D37. To take an oath. ~ SWEAR
D38. A flower. ~ ASTER
D40. What the little buds do. (Poetical.) ~ OPE
D41. These are often close, relatively speaking. ~ KIN
D42. A little word that often leads to a lot of trouble. ~ YES
D43. This runs in the Spring. ~ SAP
D44. The olden time. (Poetical.) ~ ELD
D45. That severest critic. ~ PAL
D51. This kind of girl draws interest. ~ NEAT
